WHAT THIS IS

This repository is public so that it can be read. It is not open source, and
putting it on GitHub does not make it so. This file exists because "public on
GitHub" is widely read as "free to use", and that is not what is meant here.


WHAT YOU MAY DO, WITHOUT ASKING

  - Read anything here.
  - Clone or fork the repository to read it, or to check our working.
  - Quote and cite it, with attribution, in academic work, journalism,
    teaching, or a discussion of the project.
  - Run our code on your own machine to see what it does.

WHAT NEEDS OUR WRITTEN PERMISSION FIRST

  - Redistributing this work, in whole or in part.
  - Building a derivative of it: a modified version, a project based on our
    documents, figures, analysis or code, or a product incorporating them.
  - Any commercial use.

Ask. We are not difficult about it, and we would rather be asked than not:
jacob@quis.com


WHAT IS NOT OURS TO LICENSE, AND IS NOT COVERED ABOVE

This instrument is built from two open designs that other people published,
and parts of this repository are theirs rather than ours. Nothing above grants
you any right in their work, and nothing above takes any right away from them.

  The mechanics, the controller board and the firmware follow Mech Panda's
  `red-panda-stm`. The scan head, the tip preparation and the preamplifier
  follow Dan Berard's home-built STM, at dberard.com/home-built-stm. Their
  designs belong to them. If you want to build the instrument, go to them
  first; that is where we went.

  `Code/teensy/lib/LTC2326/LTC2326_16.hpp` is Copyright (c) Daniel Berard and
  carries the full MIT licence in its header. That licence, not this file,
  governs it. Our copy changes the SPI clock and leaves his notice intact,
  which is what the MIT licence requires of a modified copy.

  `Code/teensy/src/logTable.hpp` carries Daniel Berard's copyright header,
  retained unaltered.

  `deliverables/2026-09-19-pause/figures/fonts/` contains the Inter typeface,
  Copyright (c) 2016 The Inter Project Authors, under the SIL Open Font
  License 1.1. Its own LICENSE.txt sits beside it and governs it.


A NOTE ON WHAT THIS DOES NOT CHANGE

Every measurement, every figure, every raw data file and every mistake in this
repository stays readable by anyone, for free, forever. Reserving the right to
control derivative works is not the same as hiding the results, and we are not
hiding the results. The record is the point of the project.


This file is written in plain language rather than legal language, by two
undergraduates who are not lawyers. If you need something more formal for your
own purposes, write to the address above and we will sort it out.
